# 4. Practical 2 — Inspect Network Interface Information

## Command

```bash
ip link
```

## Purpose

The `ip link` command displays information about network interfaces at the link layer.

It can show:

* Interface names
* Interface state
* MAC addresses
* Link-layer information

## What I Learned

A network interface is the communication point between a system and a network.

The command also helped me understand the difference between an interface being present and its operational state.

