# 6. Practical 4 — Test the Loopback Interface

## Command

```bash
ping -c 4 127.0.0.1
```

## Purpose

This command tests communication with the local host using the IPv4 loopback address.

```text
127.0.0.1
```

represents the same computer on which the command is being executed.

## What I Learned

Traffic sent to `127.0.0.1` is local to the host.

It does not need to travel to another physical device on the network.

The successful loopback test demonstrated that the local system could respond to ICMP requests directed at itself.

