# 12. Troubleshooting Lesson

During the practical, I also encountered network connectivity and DNS-resolution issues in my Linux environment.

This helped me understand that networking problems can occur at different layers.

For example:

```text
Application
    ↓
DNS resolution
    ↓
IP connectivity
    ↓
Routing
    ↓
Network interface
```

A problem with DNS resolution is not necessarily the same as a problem with IP connectivity.

This reinforced the importance of troubleshooting networking problems systematically instead of assuming that every failure has the same cause.

